1
00:00:00,017 --> 00:00:02,200
When a car
goes into water,

2
00:00:02,220 --> 00:00:04,240
you get about
one minute.

3
00:00:04,457 --> 00:00:07,347
The first night after
the clocks went back,

4
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:09,732
it got dark
an hour earlier.

5
00:00:09,849 --> 00:00:12,069
The car hit the water —

6
00:00:12,089 --> 00:00:13,019
and floated.

7
00:00:13,236 --> 00:00:14,667
In tests, cars floated

8
00:00:14,687 --> 00:00:16,845
about fifteen
seconds to a minute

9
00:00:16,865 --> 00:00:18,862
before water
reached the windows.

10
00:00:19,079 --> 00:00:19,881
[OWEN] The door.

11
00:00:19,901 --> 00:00:21,316
[OWEN] Get the door.

12
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:23,739
Water was pressing
on the door.

13
00:00:23,759 --> 00:00:27,280
It wouldn't open until
the car was nearly full.

14
00:00:27,497 --> 00:00:28,912
Door, or window?

15
00:00:29,447 --> 00:00:31,980
The way out
is the window —

16
00:00:31,1000 --> 00:00:34,371
while the car
is still floating.

17
00:00:34,488 --> 00:00:35,370
Belt off.

18
00:00:35,390 --> 00:00:36,024
Window.

19
00:00:37,738 --> 00:00:38,831
Then out —

20
00:00:38,851 --> 00:00:41,259
before the water
reached the glass.

21
00:00:47,176 --> 00:00:49,017
Most people
try the door.

22
00:00:49,037 --> 00:00:51,251
The ones who make it out

23
00:00:51,271 --> 00:00:52,571
use the window.

24
00:00:56,438 --> 00:00:57,822
Send this to someone

25
00:00:57,842 --> 00:00:59,428
who drives at night.

